WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.235
-Anthony,
welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.402
It's always great
to see you, bud.

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:04.804
You look great.
-Thank you.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.205
Always -- Always a pleasure
being here with you, Jimmy.

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:08.140
-You're in New York,
and I heard that you got to do

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.009
a little golf,
which I'm excited about.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:11.544
-I did.
-'Cause I -- you're a good --

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.413
you're a great golfer.
-I'm a decent golfer.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.248
-And you're fun to play with.
-That I am.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.783
-Yes.
And how did you do?

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:19.819
-We took third place.
-That's not bad.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.655
-Yeah, I played in CC --
CC Sabathia's golf tournament

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.958
this past Monday.
-Oh, I love what he does.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:27.527
-Yeah, up at
Alpine Country Club.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:30.730
It rained on us.
Poured on us.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.398
-Did it really?
-So we only got to finish

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.967
14 holes, but we were 9 under.

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:37.436
And we thought,
"9 under could actually win it."

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:40.172
Well, we found out 9 under took
third place, which isn't bad.

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:42.742
So the awards ceremony,
at the end of the day,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:47.012
in the rain, under a tent, they
announced seventh-place winner,

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:48.247
sixth-place winner,
fifth-place winner,

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:49.548
fourth-place winner,
but when they --

00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:52.118
before they got that --
they got to Worst Golfer.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.620
Worst Golfer
went to my boy, Ebro,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.989
who's a radio personality here.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:00.893
-Worst Golfer
got an all-expense trip --

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.262
all-expense-paid trip
to the Bahamas.

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:05.064
[ Laughter ]
-Wait. Worst Golfer?

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.800
-Where the hell do you give the
worst golfer a free trip...

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.735
[ Laughter ]
...to the Bahamas,

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:11.537
to stay at Baha Mar?
-What?!

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.039
-Where do you do that at?!
-What?!

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:17.076
-And $500 spa credits a day
for a four-day trip!

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.111
-Wait. What?
-Worst Golfer should get

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:20.479
golf lessons!
Am I correct?!

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:23.983
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.818
-Wait. What?
-They gave Ebro

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:29.221
a four-day vacation to the
Bahamas and $500 credit a day.

00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:30.956
-What did third place get?

00:01:30.956 --> 00:01:33.359
-An umbrella.
-Oh, this is insane.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:36.529
-Seventh place got an umbrella,
sixth place got an umbrella.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.299
fifth place got an umbrella,
fourth place got an umbrella...

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.201
-In the rain.
-...third place got an umbrella,

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:44.437
second place got an umbrella,
first place got an umbrella!

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.038
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:47.540
-And it rained that day.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.841
You could've used
the umbrella earlier.

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:50.676
-Could've used the day.
I-I don't know if they got

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:51.877
a deal on the umbrellas
that day.

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:53.246
[ Laughter ]
It's like, "We're just gonna

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.081
give this to everybody,
but what we really gonna give

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.749
is the worst golfer
a trip to the Bahamas."

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:59.285
-The Bahamas. Gosh.
Can he bring us?

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.787
-I hope so.
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.822
-I'm tagging along.
-How's --

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.590
Dude, remember last time?
We were talking about you

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.759
going back to school
and finishing your degree.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:07.960
-Yes.
-And you went to --

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.528
is it Howard?
-Howard University.

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:10.663
-That's right.
-Yes, sir.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.897
-How's that going?
Are you still doing that?

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:12.932
[ Applause ]
-Thank you.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:15.101
It's -- It's going well.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:18.404
I got a call
about a month or so ago

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.873
that I had fulfilled
my requirements.

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:22.074
-No way.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:23.709
-Hey, bud. Yeah!
-Thank you.

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:25.078
-That's what I'm talking about,
buddy.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.046
-I have fulfilled
my requirements.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.182
I think I have one class
to take in the spring,

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:33.586
but I will be walking, spring
2022, to get my degree.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.753
I started --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.753 --> 00:02:36.756
Thank you.
-That's the best, buddy.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:41.227
-I started Howard University
as a freshman, 1988.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.295
[ Laughter ]
-Is that right?

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.830
-Yeah, 1988.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.399
Getting my degree from Howard,
2022.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.666
-Yeah, that's the best.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:48.935
-You do the math.
-You do the --

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.903
-You do the math.
I don't know, carry the one.

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:52.071
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly.
-If you do the math,

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.606
you add this over here.
I don't know.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.008
It's a lot.
-I love that you did it, though.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.642
You know, you're like,
"Yeah, I'm gonna do it."

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:57.710
-Yeah.
-And then you did it.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.679
-Yeah, 30 --
I think 34 years, yeah.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.281
Yeah, some people never go back,
but, you know, my children

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:04.817
inspired me once they
went to college, and I was like,

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.752
"Yo, I'm gonna go back
and get my degree."

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:09.255
-I want to say congrats, also,
on "Black-ish."

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.157
This is the final season.
-Yeah.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:14.126
-And you've been nominated
11 times and --

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:16.462
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:19.666
-Thank you. Uh, ask me
how many times I've won.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.636
-Did you get an umbrella?
-I'm the black Susan Lucci.

00:03:24.636 --> 00:03:27.172
-Did you --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:29.508
Susan Lucci, I love it.
-I'll tell you why --

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:31.211
I'll tell you why --
that you're so good

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.612
and you get nominated
for the Emmys.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.914
Because you do something
that no one else does.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:38.617
You're funny.
You're so funny in this show,

00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:40.686
but then, you can also turn it
and make it emotional

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:42.321
in, like, the drop of a hat.
-Thank you.

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:44.356
-And it's amazing,
the talent you have, and I --

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:46.559
Honestly, there's no one
out there doing that like you.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.160
You're fantastic.
-Oh, thank you, Jimmy.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.562
I appreciate that.
-I mean it.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:53.032
-Thank you, brother, yeah.
-No one else -- it's amazing.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:57.036
But the final --
the final season, this is --

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.304
-Yeah.
-It's emotional, huh?

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.306
-It's emotional.
It's bittersweet right now.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.875
We're a little more than
halfway done with the season.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.378
Now sadness is starting
to creep in,

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:08.147
because every day we go to work,
it's one day closer

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:11.016
to bringing that -- that chapter
of all of our lives to an end.

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:14.820
So, yeah, it's getting sad now.
-You've done such great work,

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.789
and there's, like,
important shows, as well.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.225
-Yeah.
-Any hints on the final show,

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.426
or you can't give it away?
-I can't tell you that,

00:04:21.426 --> 00:04:24.730
but it is presidential.
I'll just leave it at that.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.031
-Wow. That's a good --
-Yeah.

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:27.633
That's a good hint.
-Yeah, I'll leave it at that.

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:28.867
Has nothing to do
with this president, though,

00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:30.336
but it's presidential.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.137
But it's interesting.
Sometimes people come on, I go,

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:33.305
"Can you give us a hint?"
and they go,

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:34.440
"Yeah, I can't say anything."
-No.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.541
-You just gave us
a little something.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:36.575
-I'll give you
a little something.

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:37.777
-Thank you.
I appreciate that.

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:38.844
-Yeah, don't know if it's
true or not, but okay.

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:41.246
[ Laughter ]
-I got to finally --

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:44.684
Oh, I met -- but I got to see
your mom backstage...

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:45.885
-Yeah.
-...Doris, who I love...

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.486
-Yeah.
-...who I think is, you know,

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:51.290
Well...
-She's a star in her own right.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.658
-She is the star.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:54.127
[ Laughter ]
Come on.

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.627
She is unbelievable.
-Jimmy -- Jimmy, don't --

00:04:55.627 --> 00:04:56.929
Don't contribute to that.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.865
You're throwing gasoline
on the monster fire

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:01.233
that I've created with my mom.
-That you created with your mom.

00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:02.802
But your mom is un--
-She's a monster.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:05.170
-Doris, is -- is this
Doris is here, right?

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.707
-Mom, where are you?
-Is she in the -- that's Doris.

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.408
[ Cheers and applause ]
Look at this.

00:05:09.408 --> 00:05:11.444
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:13.579
Gorgeous.

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.247
And next to --
next to your mom...

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:17.417
-Next to my mom is my son.
Take your mask off, son.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.118
Let the world
see your pretty face.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.886
Son, they're putting
cameras on you, son.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:22.822
Say what's up.
-I'm all right.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:23.856
I'm whatever.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.925
-Yeah, all right.
-My grandbaby.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.661
-Yeah.
-That's right.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:32.064
Doris, I have to say --
Oh, obviously, you're proud of

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:34.567
your son, but, man, oh, man,
we have discovered

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:37.370
something amazing in you.
I know --

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.872
-Me too.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:42.474
-"Me too."
-[ Laughing ]

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:46.145
-Doris, I heard that you have
a new -- a new boyfriend.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.246
Is that true?
-Yeah.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:48.347
-Yeah?
How's that going?

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:51.450
[ Laughter ]
-His name is Irving Theal.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.119
He's a pilot.
-Oh, really?

00:05:54.119 --> 00:05:55.321
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:59.125
-33 years at American Airlines.
-Hey!

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:00.492
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.492 --> 00:06:01.960
That's not bad.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.398
-It don't work!
It don't work!

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:11.837
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:13.873
Sorry, Irving!
It don't work!

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.741
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:18.611
That's what my mama say!
-Don't say -- now, that's --

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:21.681
-My mama say it don't work!
-That was between us!

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:24.083
That was between --
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:26.819
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.454
Now I wanna --
-Came to me, talking about,

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:29.956
"You gonna call me daddy."
No, I ain't!

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:31.157
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:33.326
I'mma tell the world --
"It don't work!"

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:36.328
-Oh, my God.

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:38.397
Everything's adjustable.
Everything's adjustable.

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:41.133
[ Laughter ]
We'll talk about it.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.369
I want to talk about the new --
your new show.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:45.071
It's a prank show called
"House Haunters."

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:47.072
-Yes.
-It's on Discovery+,

00:06:47.072 --> 00:06:48.975
and I think it's a great idea.

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:51.243
How did the idea come about
to work with your mom on this?

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:53.078
-You know,
Discovery+ came to me,

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:55.414
said, "We got this idea."
We want to do our version

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:56.816
of a prank show,
"House Haunters,"

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:58.551
and we want you
and your mother to do it."

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:00.619
I said, "Let me call my mom,
see if she's available."

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:02.554
Before I could get a --
she said, "Yeah, where we going?

00:07:02.554 --> 00:07:04.490
When we doing it?
When we going?"

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:05.791
[ Laughter ]
I said --

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:07.192
I said, "Okay, Mommy,
you don't have to worry.

00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:08.794
You're not worried about
getting paid or anything?"

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:10.062
"Yeah, you gonna
take care of me.

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:12.030
You gonna make sure I get paid.
When do we go?"

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.365
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:16.135
-So we shot it here in New York
earlier this summer.

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:20.906
Six fantastic homes that they --
they rigged with cameras

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:23.642
and booby-trapped
with a lot of excitement

00:07:23.642 --> 00:07:27.713
and just invited prospective
buyers, interior decorators,

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:30.449
Realtors in who had no idea
what was going on.

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.918
And we surprised them
with pranks with snakes --

00:07:32.918 --> 00:07:37.223
14-, 15-foot-long pythons.

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:39.425
It was --
It was amazing.

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:41.360
-Speaking of that,
it don't work.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.495
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.495 --> 00:07:48.333
All right, sorry.
But you know what I like

00:07:48.333 --> 00:07:51.370
about Discovery+,
I think what they do is they --

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.138
they make, like,
appointment television.

00:07:53.138 --> 00:07:54.373
-Yes.
-Like, I mean, you --

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:56.008
So it's perfect for now.
It's October.

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:58.444
People want to get scared.
I want to show everyone.

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:00.646
It's very funny.
Here's Anthony Anderson

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.915
and his beautiful mom, Doris,
in "House Haunters."

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.450
Take a look.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.890
-Bring in the girl.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:13.192
-Come here.
-No!

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:14.827
[ Screaming ]

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:18.130
-[ Laughing ]

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:21.233
-And what the hell?
Oh.

00:08:21.233 --> 00:08:24.036
It's crazy.
It's creepy.

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:25.871
♪♪

00:08:25.871 --> 00:08:28.273
-[ Screaming ]

00:08:28.273 --> 00:08:30.743
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:36.681
-I watch you sleep.
[ Laughs ]

00:08:36.681 --> 00:08:37.950
-What do we do?

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.053
-Uh, just fight it, I guess?
-Let's go, mama.

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:43.622
Let's go, let's go.
Let's go.

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:45.891
-"Fight it, I guess"?
What is he talking about?

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:48.127
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Sometimes they didn't work.

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:49.795
-It's that laugh
that is the best.

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:51.730
-Sometimes it didn't work.
-Anthony Anderson, everybody.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:55.568
"House Haunters" premieres
tomorrow on Discovery+.

